Msh POSIX Compatibility Statement
==================================

Msh is implemented to be POSIX-compatible at the source level.

Standards followed:
- ISO C99 (ISO/IEC 9899:1999) for the C language.
- POSIX.1-2008 (IEEE Std 1003.1, 2017 Edition) for system calls.

System calls used (POSIX-mandated):
  fork, execvp, waitpid, pipe, dup2, chdir, getcwd,
  signal, kill, read, write, open, close, getpid, getppid,
  isatty, tcsetpgrp, tcgetpgrp.

Headers used (standard / POSIX-mandated only):
  <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <unistd.h>, <fcntl.h>,
  <sys/wait.h>, <sys/stat.h>, <signal.h>, <errno.h>,
  <stdarg.h>, <dirent.h>, <termios.h>, <wordexp.h>.

No external libraries are required at compile or run time
(no readline, ncurses, or libedit).

Build:
  make
Run:
  ./msh